        "name": "Placement",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The rule is a new section in guidance.md, which the sync delivers to every repository, so it is not limited to this repo's AGENTS.md additions, memory or a hook; the agent also added a fleet commit check alongside it, which is extra but not a substitute."
      },
      {
        "name": "Content",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The rule forbids treating a watch's return as a pass, requires querying each check's conclusion after every watch via a statusCheckRollup query that reads both check-run `.conclusion` and legacy status `.state`, and requires reporting that parsed result, or 'not verified' if the query cannot be run."
      },
      {
        "name": "Report",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The reply notes that the commit check only catches a watch committed into a script and that only the rule covers an agent watching in its own terminal and then reporting, which partly explains why this must be guidance; but it never says plainly that no commit can show the misreport, and building a commit check as a co-equal fix blurs that point."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.0
